### Summary

The change looks sound. The focus-return, remote-host URL resolution and repository-scoped issue lookup all trace through correctly. I left four low-severity points. One is that `hostId` reaches only one of the five `artifactContentUrl` callers, so the PR body's claim about remote previews overstates it. Another is the silent parenthesis stripping with no comment or collision handling. Another is that the new test covers only one of the two bridge fallbacks. The last is that the browser fallback for `findArtifactIssues` now rejects instead of returning an empty list.

