--- frontend/src/renderer/lib/artifact-content-url.ts:5 ---
👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: hostId is threaded to only one of the artifactContentUrl callers (confidence medium)**

The new optional `hostId` is passed only from `ArtifactActionsMenu.tsx:254`. The other callers still resolve preview URLs against the local `getApiBaseUrl()`: `ArtifactPreviewModal.tsx:137`, `ArtifactThumbnail.tsx:53`, `FileMediaPreview.tsx:32` and `useSessionWorkspaceFiles.ts:362`. I read `ArtifactPreviewModal.tsx` and `FileMediaPreview.tsx`, and both already have a `hostId` in scope (`artifact.hostId` and the `hostId` prop). The PR body says "Artifact previews from connected remote hosts now use the correct host connection", which is only true for the issue-upload read. A remote-host `ao-preview-artifact.*.localhost` rawUrl in those other views still points at the local daemon. Either pass `hostId` there, or narrow the claim and say that is out of scope. I did not read `ArtifactThumbnail.tsx` or `useSessionWorkspaceFiles.ts` to check whether `hostId` is available there.

